---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import GoogleBusinessInfo from '../../components/GoogleBusinessInfo.astro';

const title = 'Mason City Drain Cleaning | A-1 Drain Cleaning';
const description = 'Mason City, IA drain cleaning for backed-up basement floor drains, clogged main drains, sewer lines, toilets, sinks, tubs and showers. A-1 Drain Cleaning. Call 641-530-2728.';
---

<MainLayout title={title} description={description} path="/mason-city-drain-cleaning/">
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="bg-[#1A1A68] text-white">
      <div class="container grid gap-10 py-14 sm:py-18 lg:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr] lg:items-center lg:py-20">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-red-300">A-1 Drain Cleaning • Mason City, Iowa</p>
          <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-4xl text-5xl font-black leading-[.98] tracking-tight sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">Mason City Drain Cleaning</h1>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-200 sm:text-xl">A-1 Drain Cleaning is based in Mason City, Iowa. We clear clogged household drains, main drains, basement floor drains, laundry drains and sewer lines for Mason City homes and businesses. If sewage is coming up through a floor drain, several fixtures are backing up, or one sink or toilet will not drain, call 641-530-2728.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-200">One slow sink is a different problem from sewage coming up through a basement floor drain. Tell us which fixture is affected, whether more than one drain is involved, and what was running when the backup started. Those details help narrow down whether the restriction is at one fixture, in a shared branch, or farther down the main drain or sewer line.</p>
          <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="mt-8 inline-block rounded-md bg-[#c52b34] px-7 py-4 text-center text-lg font-black text-white hover:bg-[#a82129]">CALL 641-530-2728</a>
          <p class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-300">24/7 drain and sewer service • Mason City and surrounding North Iowa</p>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-xl text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">A-1 Drain Cleaning is based at 206 29th St SW in Mason City. You can call directly and describe the problem—no need to know the name of the pipe or blockage.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="border border-white/15 bg-white/10 p-6 sm:p-8" aria-labelledby="mason-city-problem">
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-red-200">Start with the symptom</p>
          <h2 id="mason-city-problem" class="mt-3 text-3xl font-black leading-tight">What is the drain doing?</h2>
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-slate-200">
            <li class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4"><strong class="text-white">One sink, tub, or shower:</strong> slow or completely stopped.</li>
            <li class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4"><strong class="text-white">Several fixtures:</strong> more than one drain backs up or gurgles.</li>
            <li class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4"><strong class="text-white">Basement floor drain:</strong> wastewater rises when water is used elsewhere.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Laundry:</strong> washer discharge comes back through a standpipe or floor drain.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="mason-city-answers">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Mason City drain problems</p>
        <h2 id="mason-city-answers" class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">What kind of drain problem do you have?</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A single slow fixture can have a blockage close to that fixture. When several fixtures are affected, a toilet flush makes another drain rise, or wastewater comes up through the lowest drain, the restriction may be farther down a shared line or the main sewer.</p>
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Main drain backup</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">If toilets, sinks, tubs, or floor drains are affected together, the problem may be in the main drain or a shared line.</p><a href="/services/main-drain-cleaning/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Main drain cleaning →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Basement floor drain backup</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">A basement floor drain is often one of the lowest openings in the house. Wastewater there can be a sign of a downstream restriction.</p><a href="/services/basement-floor-drains/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Basement floor drains →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Sewer line blockage</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Repeated backups or a blockage farther down the sewer line can affect several fixtures at once.</p><a href="/services/sewer-line-cleaning/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Sewer line cleaning →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Kitchen and bathroom drains</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Slow or stopped sinks, tubs, and showers can have a blockage in the fixture drain or a nearby branch line.</p><a href="/services/kitchen-drains/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Kitchen drains →</a><a href="/services/bathroom-shower-drains/" class="mt-2 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Bathroom &amp; shower drains →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Laundry drain backup</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">A washing machine pumps out quickly. A restricted laundry or shared drain can cause water to rise when the washer empties.</p><a href="/services/laundry-drains/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Laundry drains →</a></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Tree roots in sewer lines</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Roots entering a sewer line can contribute to recurring blockages. Tell us if the same line keeps stopping up.</p><a href="/services/tree-roots-in-sewer-line/" class="mt-4 inline-flex font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">Tree roots in sewer lines →</a></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-slate-100 py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="mason-city-quick-answers">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Quick answers</p>
        <h2 id="mason-city-quick-answers" class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Mason City drain cleaning questions</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">How do I know if my main drain is blocked?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">Several fixtures backing up together, wastewater coming up through a basement floor drain, or one fixture causing another to rise can point to a restriction farther down the drain system. Those symptoms are clues, not a diagnosis.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">What should I do if sewage comes up through a floor drain?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">Stop using toilets, sinks, showers, and the washing machine as much as practical. Keep children and pets away from wastewater. Call A-1 Drain Cleaning at <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-2">641-530-2728</a> and explain which fixtures were being used when the backup happened.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Why does my washing machine make a floor drain back up?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A washer releases a large amount of water quickly. If the laundry drain or a shared line cannot carry that flow away, water can rise in the standpipe or come through a nearby floor drain.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Can a sewer backup happen in a house without a basement?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">Yes. In a home without a basement floor drain, a blocked main line may show up in a bathtub or shower. Tell us which fixture backed up first and whether other drains are affected.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Do you provide 24/7 drain cleaning in Mason City?</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A-1 Drain Cleaning offers 24/7 drain and sewer service. Call <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-2">641-530-2728</a> and explain the blockage or backup.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="mason-city-local">
      <div class="container grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] lg:items-start">
        <div><p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Local service</p><h2 id="mason-city-local" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Based in Mason City</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A-1 Drain Cleaning is based at 206 29th St SW, Mason City, Iowa 50401. Mason City is the home base for service in the surrounding North Iowa communities.</p><address class="mt-5 not-italic font-bold text-slate-950">206 29th St SW<br />Mason City, IA 50401</address><a href="tel:+16415302728" class="mt-6 inline-flex rounded-md bg-[#c52b34] px-6 py-3 font-black text-white hover:bg-[#a82129]">CALL 641-530-2728</a></div>
        <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><a href="/service-area/clear-lake/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Clear Lake</a><a href="/service-area/forest-city/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Forest City</a><a href="/service-area/charles-city/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Charles City</a><a href="/service-area/nora-springs/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Nora Springs</a><a href="/service-area/garner/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Garner</a><a href="/service-area/northwood/" class="border border-slate-200 p-4 font-black text-slate-950 hover:border-[#b4232b] hover:text-[#b4232b]">Northwood</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="mason-city-fixtures">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Fixture and drain service</p>
        <h2 id="mason-city-fixtures" class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Clogged toilet, sink, bathtub, shower or floor drain?</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">A-1 Drain Cleaning handles individual fixture clogs as well as larger drain and sewer blockages. A slow bathroom sink may need work on its own drain. A toilet that bubbles when the tub drains, or a floor drain that spills when laundry runs, may point to a restriction in a shared line. The pattern matters.</p>
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Toilet unclogging</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">A toilet that will not clear, repeatedly clogs, or causes nearby fixtures to gurgle may have a blockage in the toilet or farther down the drain system.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Sink drain cleaning</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Kitchen and bathroom sinks can slow down from grease, soap residue, hair and other material collecting in the drain. If other fixtures are affected too, mention that when you call.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Bathtub and shower drains</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Standing water in a tub or shower often points to a local drain restriction. If wastewater rises into the tub when another fixture runs, the problem may be farther downstream.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Basement floor drains</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Water or sewage coming up through a basement floor drain needs prompt attention. Stop running water where practical and keep people and pets away from wastewater.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Laundry and washing machine drains</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">A washer discharges quickly. A restricted laundry drain or shared line can overflow at the standpipe or push water out of a nearby floor drain.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 p-5"><h3 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Main drain and sewer lines</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">When multiple fixtures back up together, the restriction may be in a branch line, house main drain or private sewer lateral. The symptoms help determine where to investigate.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-slate-100 py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="mason-city-diagnosis">
      <div class="container grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.8fr_1.2fr] lg:items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Finding the blockage</p>
          <h2 id="mason-city-diagnosis" class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">How A-1 approaches a drain backup</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">The first step is understanding what is backing up and when it happens. A-1 Drain Cleaning uses the symptoms, access to the line and condition of the pipe to determine an appropriate cleaning or inspection method.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="space-y-4">
          <li class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><h3 class="font-black text-slate-950">1. Identify the affected fixtures</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">We need to know whether it is one sink or toilet, several fixtures, the laundry standpipe, a basement floor drain, or a tub or shower. Tell us what was running when the problem began.</p></li>
          <li class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><h3 class="font-black text-slate-950">2. Locate a suitable access point</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">The available cleanout, fixture access and layout of the drain system help determine where the line can be reached. Not every blockage is in the same place.</p></li>
          <li class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><h3 class="font-black text-slate-950">3. Clear the restriction with an appropriate method</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">Drain cable equipment, tree root removal equipment or hydro-jetting may be appropriate depending on the blockage and pipe condition. The method is selected for the line—not used automatically on every drain.</p></li>
          <li class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><h3 class="font-black text-slate-950">4. Investigate repeat problems when needed</h3><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-700">If a sewer line keeps plugging, a camera inspection can help identify roots, buildup, offsets or visible pipe damage when the line and conditions allow. A camera inspection is a diagnostic step, not a substitute for clearing a blockage.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-white py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="mason-city-private-sewer">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Know which line is affected</p>
        <h2 id="mason-city-private-sewer" class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">House drain, private sewer lateral or city sewer main?</h2>
        <div class="mt-5 max-w-4xl space-y-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">
          <p>Your home's fixture drains connect to branch piping and a larger building drain or house main. That system then connects to the private sewer lateral leading toward the public sewer. A backup inside the home does not, by itself, prove whether the blockage is in the house piping, the private lateral or the public sewer main.</p>
          <p>Several fixtures backing up together, sewage at the lowest floor drain, or a toilet causing a tub or shower to rise can indicate a restriction in a shared drain or downstream line. These are clues only. The location has to be checked before anyone can say which section is blocked.</p>
          <p>A-1 Drain Cleaning provides private drain and sewer cleaning. If the evidence points to a problem in the public sewer main rather than the property's piping, contact the City of Mason City or the appropriate sewer authority to report it. Do not assume a city-main problem is a private-line cleaning job.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-slate-100 py-14 sm:py-18" aria-labelledby="mason-city-emergency">
      <div class="container grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:items-center">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Sewage backup</p>
          <h2 id="mason-city-emergency" class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Sewage coming up through the basement floor drain?</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-slate-700">Stop using toilets, sinks, showers and the washing machine as much as practical. Additional water entering a blocked drain can make the backup worse. Keep children and pets out of the affected area, avoid direct contact with wastewater, and do not try to wash sewage down another drain.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-slate-700">When you call, say whether the water is clear or dirty, whether it rises when a toilet is flushed or the washer drains, and whether more than one fixture is affected. If the backup is active, say that first.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="inline-flex min-h-14 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-[#c52b34] px-7 py-4 text-lg font-black text-white hover:bg-[#a82129]">CALL 641-530-2728</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ContactCTA showForm />
    <GoogleBusinessInfo />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</MainLayout>
